# 25. Security and Future Backend Readiness

Follow these requirements:

- Never expose database credentials in frontend code.
- Never expose AI API keys in frontend code.
- Never store production passwords in localStorage.
- Never treat frontend role checks as authorization.
- Do not allow browser-side direct MySQL access.
- Prepare server-side authorization interfaces.
- Validate all form inputs.
- Use safe rendering for user-generated content.
- Prepare secure media upload interfaces.
- Prepare CSRF-protected backend integration.
- Prepare rate-limited chatbot and enquiry endpoints.

All sensitive operations must eventually be performed by the backend.

