# 29. Final Quality Requirements

The final result must be a complete frontend prototype, not just a collection of screenshots.

Every page must have meaningful content and a finished design.

Every dashboard section must have a working interface.

All major admin operations must be testable with demo data.

The public website must reflect changes made in the admin dashboard.

The installer must have a complete navigable flow.

The chatbot must demonstrate useful answers based on editable demo knowledge.

The project must be prepared for a custom MySQL backend without Supabase dependencies.

Do not stop after building the homepage.

Do not generate empty placeholder admin screens.

Do not use generic dashboard templates.

Do not leave buttons without actions.

Do not invent institutional approvals, placement statistics, faculty credentials or admission claims.

Use actual existing institutional content where available, and mark unverified information for administrator review.

**Final objective:** Deliver a premium, elegant, fully responsive KITS College of Pharmacy for Women website with a complete self-hosting-ready CMS frontend, powerful visual customization, chatbot management and installation wizard, ready for subsequent custom backend development.